# The grain deletes the doomed manifests in listing order instead of tip
# first, so a pass interrupted between two deletes can leave a doomed
# increment's sink manifest without its base. SinkChainIntact: a published
# increment still in the sink has a restorable base.
MODULE: BackupRetention
ROW: SinkChainIntact
FILE: src/lattice.backup/BackupSchedulerGrain.cs
DETECTORS: BackupSchedulerGrainUnitTests.PruneAsync_deletes_a_doomed_chain_tip_first
SUMMARY: a retention pass deletes a doomed base before its doomed increment

--- FIND
        foreach (var manifest in BackupRetentionPlanner.TipFirst(deleting))
--- REPLACE
        foreach (var manifest in deleting)
--- END
